msgid "Privacy First, Comfort Second: You’ve managed to block third-party access to your personal data, but comfort has taken a hit. The smart heater now requires a fingerprint scan every hour, the lights are stuck in “eco mode” dimness, and the oven refuses to preheat via the app — it seems you have to handle all the “smart” tasks yourself. At least your friends offered to bring pizza after you couldn’t store your location in the delivery app, and you open the door for them manually once they knock. Your privacy preferences are at a good level, but your Smart Home lacks the data access it needs to function properly. Next time, try to consider the consequences of specific data-access permissions for your Smart Home."
